Suffix metadata transfer mutates empty destinations
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/64d7ae25c06481918b26c8dc5e147a53?sev=&repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin
Criticality: medium
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit [`c72fd88c`](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/c72fd88c06b0fbc83710ceb8581dee5a0faeab4f) (`Reject metadata transfer suffixes on empty destinations`).

The finding was valid for the reported commit `0c4a217`: the retained-log metadata transfer import path classified an initializable zero-log destination as `Empty` before checking whether the artifact was a true suffix with a non-zero base proof. The `Empty` branch could then replay suffix commands against an empty materialized metadata store and detect the proof mismatch only after mutation, leaving the destination dirty.

The fix makes empty-destination classification prove that the destination's current zero-log proof exactly matches the artifact base proof before returning `MetadataTransferImportDestination::Empty`. Complete-prefix and empty-state imports still work because their base proof is the canonical zero-log destination proof, but true suffix artifacts now require an existing proven base/prefix or fail closed before any replay. A new regression, `metadata_transfer_import_rejects_suffix_into_empty_destination_without_mutation`, constructs a real retained suffix artifact by dropping the first retained log entry, attempts import into empty destination replicas, and verifies both replicas remain at log index/hash `0` with no suffix bucket after rejection.

Verification for the resolution:
- `cargo test -p storage metadata_transfer -- --nocapture`
- `bash -n scripts/uat-s3-tests`
- `cargo nextest run` passed 5601 tests.

